The vision_opencv repository should be cloned into your ROS 2 workspace, typically located in a directory like ~/ros2_ws/src or ~/Documents/opencv_ros2_ws/src. Here's how you can properly clone and set it up:

Steps to Clone and Build vision_opencv
Navigate to Your ROS 2 Workspace If your workspace is ~/Documents/opencv_ros2_ws, navigate to its src directory:

bash
Kodu kopyala
cd ~/quadcopter_drone_ws/src
Clone the Repository Clone the vision_opencv repository into the src directory:

bash

git clone https://github.com/ros-perception/vision_opencv.git
Checkout the Correct Branch Since you're using ROS 2 Humble, checkout the humble branch:

bash
Kodu kopyala
cd vision_opencv
git checkout humble
Return to the Workspace Root Go back to the root of your workspace:

bash
Kodu kopyala
cd ~/Documents/opencv_ros2_ws
Build the Workspace Build the vision_opencv package with the correct OpenCV version:

bash
Kodu kopyala
colcon build --packages-select cv_bridge --cmake-args -DOpenCV_DIR=/usr/local/lib/cmake/opencv4



Replace /path/to/opencv4.11/cmake with the actual path to OpenCV 4.11's CMake configuration files (e.g., /usr/local/lib/cmake/opencv4)




--------------------------------
Verify the Installation
After building, ensure the OpenCV version linked by cv_bridge is correct. You can check by inspecting the logs or running the cv_bridge node to see if it recognizes the installed OpenCV version.

If everything builds and links correctly, you can proceed to build your yolo_opencv package.





Verify Integration with Your yolo_opencv Package
Ensure cv_bridge builds successfully.
After building, you can build your yolo_opencv package:
bash
Kodu kopyala
colcon build --packages-select yolo_opencv --cmake-args -DOpenCV_DIR=/usr/local/lib/cmake/opencv4
This setup ensures that the cv_bridge package from vision_opencv is properly integrated with your workspace and uses your custom OpenCV installation.




source ~/Documents/opencv_ros2_ws/install/setup.bash



colcon build --packages-select cv_bridge --cmake-args -DOpenCV_DIR=/usr/local/lib/cmake/opencv4


colcon build --packages-select yolo_opencv --cmake-clean-cache
ros2 run yolo_opencv yolo_detection_node --ros-args -p use_cuda:=true


